<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 3 Best in Slot Gear list for Shadow Priest DPS in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Trial of the Grand Crusader. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Shadow Priest DPS Phase 3</h2>While there isn't much of a difference when it comes to gearing race to race, it is important to note that Alliance Priests with a Draenei in their party will only need 10% Hit from gear, as opposed to the 11% Horde races will need. <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=26297/berserking">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/racial_troll_berserk.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Berserking</span></a> also shifts the weight of stats a little, but rarely enough to gear around being Troll vs Undead or Blood Elf.<br/>
<br/>
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/side_horde.gif");'></span>Horde Priests will need to grab Hit where they can to make sure they hit the cap. Items like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47467/dark-essence-bindings">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_32a.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dark Essence Bindings</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45294/petrified-ivy-sprig">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_wand_29.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Petrified Ivy Sprig</span></a> are solid choices with minimal stat loss. It is also worth noting that the Healer versions of Tier 9 are not bad items individually, just that the set bonus does not give us anything. Sometimes the difference between a healer and DPS piece is Crit Rating vs Hit Rating.<br/>
<br/>Ideally you will always want to maintain your 4 set bonus from <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-180/triumphant-velens-regalia">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Triumphant Velen's Regalia</span></a>, so if you decide to use a non-Tier piece in a slot, you will want to make up for it elsewhere if possible. Using an item level 245 Tier piece to keep a set bonus is likely always going to be more valuable than using an item level 258 piece in that slot and losing the bonus.<div class="pad"></div>
