<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="rings">Rings for Shadow Priest DPS Phase 3</h3>If you got your hands on good rings in Phase 2, you can just coast in Phase 3, though there is at least one upgrade available.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45495/conductive-seal">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_66.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Conductive Seal</span></a> is another simple choice, an item level 252 ring with no wasted stats and a socket. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46046/nebula-band">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_70.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nebula Band</span></a> on the other hand isn't the highest item level option, but it is close enough and again, has no wasted stats and a socket. If you find yourself hurting for hit, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45297/shimmering-seal">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_63.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shimmering Seal</span></a> is also a very solid option, but does sacrifice a decent chunk of stats for hit.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Ring Enchant</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=44636/enchant-ring-greater-spellpower">
